Copyright (c) 2026 Mitchell Lorin. All rights reserved.

**This is not open source.** No part of this repository is licensed for public use,
modification or redistribution. It is licensed to one client at a time, under the terms
below, and every copy of it remains the property of the copyright holder.

> **Plain-English summary — not the agreement.** A manufacturer pays to run a branded
> instance of this software for its own business and its own dealers. It may not resell
> the software, publish it as its own product, or hand copies of the source to anyone
> else. The manufacturer owns its catalogue and its designs; the engine stays ours. The
> quotes it produces are illustrative and must be verified before anyone cuts material or
> sends a customer a price. The numbered terms below govern.

**Not legal advice.** This document was drafted as a starting point, not by a lawyer, and
no warranty is given as to its fitness for any particular jurisdiction. Have it reviewed
before you sign or send it to a client. Square-bracketed fields are filled in per
engagement.

---

## 1. Definitions

**"Software"** — the source code, documentation and catalogue-format specification in
this repository, including the rules engine, the studio interface, the deployment tooling
and any updates supplied under § 6.

**"Licensor"** — the copyright holder named above.

**"Licensee"** — the single legal entity named in the Order that accepts these terms.

**"Order"** — the written quotation, offer sheet or purchase order that identifies the
Licensee, the fees, the term and any Catalogue Work under § 4.

**"Instance"** — one deployment of the Software, serving one brand at one origin, as
described in `DEPLOY.md`.

**"Licensee Catalogue"** — the catalogue documents (§ 3) and any other data describing
the Licensee's products: dimensions, materials, hardware, pricing, product families.

**"Dealer"** — a business the Licensee authorises to use its Instance, identified by an
access code configured under § 5.

## 2. Licence grant

2.1 Subject to payment of the fees in the Order and to the restrictions in § 3, the
Licensor grants the Licensee a **non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable,
worldwide** licence, for the term stated in the Order, to:

  (a) deploy and run the number of Instances stated in the Order, branded to the
      Licensee, for the Licensee's own internal business purposes;

  (b) enable its Dealers to use those Instances to configure products, price them and
      produce documents for the Licensee's and their own customers;

  (c) make a reasonable number of copies of the Software for backup, testing and
      disaster recovery.

2.2 **Source access is not a grant.** Where the Licensee receives the source (as on
delivery), it receives it to run and configure the Instance and to write its own
catalogue documents. No other right in the source is granted.

2.3 All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Licensor.

## 3. Restrictions

The Licensee shall not, and shall not permit any third party to:

  (a) sell, resell, rent, lease, sublicense, distribute or otherwise make the Software
      available to any person other than its Dealers and its own personnel, or operate it
      as a service for third parties;

  (b) publish, disclose or make the source available, in whole or in part, except to
      personnel and contractors bound by written confidentiality obligations at least as
      protective as these terms;

  (c) use the Software, or any part of its design, to develop, market or supply a
      competing product configurator, or to benchmark or publish performance comparisons
      without the Licensor's written consent;

  (d) remove, obscure or alter any copyright, attribution or licence notice in the
      Software, or present the Software as its own product where the Licensor's
      authorship is material to the deal;

  (e) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except to the extent that
      this restriction is prohibited by applicable law, or use it to build a substantially
      similar product;

  (f) use the Software to produce any document that the Licensee presents as a binding
      manufacturer quotation, or as a bill of materials for production, without the
      verification required by § 7.

**Dealer codes are the Licensee's responsibility.** The Licensee shall issue access codes
only to businesses it has authorised, keep them confidential, revoke them when the
relationship ends, and notify the Licensor promptly of any suspected misuse.

## 4. Catalogue work and ownership

4.1 **The Licensee owns its Catalogue.** All Licensee Catalogue documents, and all
designs, layouts and customer records created in the Instance, remain the Licensee's
property. The Licensor claims no licence over them beyond what is needed to operate the
Instance and to provide the services in the Order.

4.2 **The Licensor owns the engine.** The Software, its architecture, its rules engine,
its catalogue *format* and specification, and all improvements to any of them, remain the
Licensor's property. Writing a catalogue document under the published schema does not
create any interest in the engine.

4.3 Where the Licensor performs **Catalogue Work** — digitising product families into
catalogue documents — the resulting documents are delivered to the Licensee and owned by
it. The Licensor may retain and reuse the *techniques* used to produce them, but not the
Licensee's catalogue data, dimensions, pricing or product names.

4.4 On termination, the Licensor shall make the Licensee's Catalogue and design data
available for export in a machine-readable format, and shall delete its own copies within
[30] days of a written request, save for copies required by law or held in routine
backups.

## 5. Dealer accounts and pricing tiers

5.1 Dealer accounts, their access codes and their price tiers are configured in the
Instance by the Licensee (see `DEPLOY.md` § 6). The Licensor does not set, verify or
police the Licensee's dealer pricing.

5.2 The Licensee is responsible for the accuracy of every tier, discount and price in its
arrangement, and for what its Dealers charge their own customers.

5.3 Access codes are stored in configuration, not in a licence-management service. A code
is valid until it is removed from the configuration and the Instance is redeployed; there
is no self-service signup, password reset or session expiry, and none is promised.

## 6. Support, updates and term

6.1 During the term, the Licensor shall provide [the support stated in the Order], and
shall supply updates to the Software that it makes generally available to its licensees.

6.2 Unless the Order says otherwise, the term is [12 months] from delivery, renewing for
successive [12-month] periods unless either party gives [30] days' written notice.

6.3 Each catalogue **price refresh** — updating the Licensee's catalogue when its price
list, hardware or product families change — is part of the recurring service and is
covered by the recurring fee for up to [one] refresh per [quarter], or as stated in the
Order.

## 7. Illustrative pricing — the warranty that matters most

7.1 Prices produced by the Software are **illustrative**. They are built from the
Licensee's catalogue rates and a set of stated assumptions, including surface rates,
labour and finishing allowances. They are not a manufacturer quotation and are not an
offer to sell.

7.2 **The Licensee is responsible for verifying** every figure and every production
document before it is relied on — including cut sizes, machining, edge banding, part
counts and totals — against its own engineering and pricing systems. The `QuotePage`
output, the production BOM export and the CSV export all carry a disclaimer saying so and
that disclaimer is a term of this licence.

7.3 The Software is not a substitute for the Licensee's design, estimating, engineering
or production systems, and is not warranted to produce a manufacturable result.

## 8. Fees

8.1 Fees, currency and payment terms are as stated in the Order. One-off fees for
deployment and Catalogue Work are payable [on delivery]; recurring fees are payable
[annually in advance].

8.2 Late payment may result in suspension of the Instance after [14] days' written
notice. The Licensee's Catalogue and design data shall be exported to it under § 4.4
before any deletion.

8.3 Fees are exclusive of taxes.

## 9. Warranty and disclaimer

9.1 The Licensor warrants that it has the right to grant this licence, and that the
Software will perform substantially as described in the documentation supplied with it
for [30] days from delivery.

9.2 **Except as stated in § 9.1, the Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
kind, express or implied, including any implied warranty of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose, accuracy of pricing, or non-infringement.** The Licensor does not
warrant that the Software will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that any price, cut list
or production document it produces is correct.

9.3 The Licensee's sole remedy for breach of § 9.1 is repair, replacement or refund of the
fees paid for the affected period, at the Licensor's option.

## 10. Limitation of liability

10.1 Neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss,
loss of profit, loss of business, loss of data or business interruption, however caused.

10.2 The Licensor's total aggregate liability under or in connection with this agreement
is limited to the fees paid by the Licensee in the [12] months preceding the claim.

10.3 Nothing limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or
any liability that cannot lawfully be limited.

## 11. Termination

11.1 Either party may terminate for material breach not remedied within [30] days of
written notice, or immediately on the other's insolvency.

11.2 On termination the Licensee shall stop using the Software, delete or return the
source and any copies, and destroy or confirm deletion of all Instances, except that it
may retain its own Catalogue and exported data under § 4.4.

## 12. General

12.1 **Entire agreement.** This licence and the Order are the whole agreement and
supersede prior discussions.

12.2 **Assignment.** The Licensee may not assign this agreement without the Licensor's
